==Levels and Stages==
The only stages were the three [[Empire of Cats]] Chapters and the [[Higher Score|Challenge Battle]].

The Main Chapters took place in Japan, with each of the stages named after a prefecture in Japan except for stage 48, which was [[wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]]. All of the names, [[Enemy Bases|enemy bases]], [[Treasure]]s and [[Backgrounds|backgrounds]] were the same as those still used in [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]].

==Trivia==
*Despite it being "taken down", the game was instead updated in Japan to become the current [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]].
*[[Madagascar (Empire of Cats)|Stage 16]] was incorrectly named Shimatori rather than [[wikipedia:Tottori Prefecture|Tottori]].
*[[Ms. Sign]] being a slut could be a nod to her Japanese name, Kanban Musume, which literally translates to "Signboard Girl" but can also refer to an attractive girl who stands outside a store to attract customers.
*[[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Frog Ninja Cat]]'s description uses male pronouns when referring to her. This was changed in the 2014 release, and she was later confirmed to be female in [[The Burgle Cats]].

